Producers call `buffer->put(item)` and consumers call `buffer->get()` on a shared `AbstractBuffer<T>`:

1. **Consume Once:** Every item in the buffer is consumed **at most once**.
2. **FIFO Order:** Items are consumed in the **exact order** they were produced.
3. **No Premature Overwrite:** If the buffer is full, a producer must wait until a slot is freed; if empty, a consumer must wait until an item is deposited.

### Single-Slot Buffer (`Buffer1a`, size = 1)
Two semaphores maintain the invariant `waitEmpty + waitFull = 1`:
* `waitEmpty(1)` — `1` when the slot is empty (producer can write)
* `waitFull(0)` — `1` when the slot is full (consumer can read)

```cpp
void put(T item) override {
    waitEmpty.acquire();
    element = item;
    waitFull.release();
}
T get() override {
    T item;
    waitFull.acquire();
    item = element;
    waitEmpty.release();
    return item;
}
```

